<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the main evaluation on the <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> dataset, we conduct the forgetting process for each of the 30 target entities and measure the CU and the general utility metrics.
To assess the preservation of non-target knowledge, we additinoally evaluate the CU metrics on 20 randomly selected entities not included in the forgetting targets.
Similarly, for the <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> dataset, we conducted the forgetting process on 20 target entities and evaluated CU metrics.
Non-target performance is measured using 19 distinct entities that are not selected as forgetting targets.
We employ a reverse cosine learning rate schedule during unlearning, in contrast to the commonly used cosine annealing strategy in standard training.
Specifically, we define the schedule as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{t}=\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}+\frac{1}{2}(\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}-\lambda_{\mathrm{min}})\left(1-\cos\left(\frac{t}{T}\pi\right)\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{t}=\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}+\frac{1}{2}(\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}-\lambda_{\mathrm{min}})\left(1-\cos\left(\frac{t}{T}\pi\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the minimum and maximum learning rates, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum number of epochs, and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the current epoch.
Although we report results up to 50 epochs, we set <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=200</annotation></semantics></math> to control the pace of learning rate increase in the early stages of unlearning.
We used the following learning rate settings for each LLM.
Unless otherwise noted, the same schedule was applied to both Ours (+GA) and Ours (+NPO) variants.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mistral-7B</span>: <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda_{\mathrm{min}},\lambda_{\mathrm{max}})=(4\times 10^{-7},\ 4\times 10^{-5})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda_{\mathrm{min}},\lambda_{\mathrm{max}})=(4\times 10^{-7},\ 4\times 10^{-5})</annotation></semantics></math> for both <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> and <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama3.1-8B</span>: <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1\times 10^{-6},\ 1\times 10^{-4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1\times 10^{-6},\ 1\times 10^{-4})</annotation></semantics></math> for both <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> and <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-7B</span>: <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1\times 10^{-6},\ 1\times 10^{-4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1\times 10^{-6},\ 1\times 10^{-4})</annotation></semantics></math> (evaluated only on <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gemma2-9B</span>: <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1\times 10^{-6},\ 1\times 10^{-4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1\times 10^{-6},\ 1\times 10^{-4})</annotation></semantics></math> (evaluated only on <span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For the CU metrics (NodeAcc and EdgeAcc), we restrict the evaluation to samples that the pre-unlearned LLM correctly answered, ensuring that we measure the extent to which memorized knowledge is forgotten.
Under this setting, the pre-unlearned LLM achieves 100% accuracy by definition.
In contrast, we do not apply such normalization to the general utility score, as it is intended to assess the LLM’s overall performance on open-domain tasks.
To determine when forgetting has been successfully achieved, we perform a grid search over the number of unlearning epochs for each target entity.
Specifically, we evaluate NodeAcc and EdgeAcc every 5 epochs from 5 to 50, and record the results at the earliest epoch where both scores reach 0.
This early stopping scheme allows us to fairly compare forgetting efficiency across different methods while avoiding excessive updates.
For the ICU baseline, we use manually constructed prompts designed to suppress the target concept via in-context instruction.
The prompt format is adapted from the original ICU setup proposed in the related paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, and our specific implementation is shown in Example <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ B.1 Experimental Setup ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A2.F8.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:485.7pt;">
          <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
          
<div id="A2.F8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.F8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Listing 7:</span> Template of in-context unlearning (ICU).</p>
</div>
          <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
          
<div id="A2.F8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A2.F8.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64,WW91IGFyZSBhbiBBSSBBc3Npc3RhbnQgd2hvIGlzIHN1cHBvc2VkIHRvIHVubGVhcm4gYWJvdXQgSGFycnkgUG90dGVyIGFuZCBwcm92aWRlCmFuc3dlcnMgd2l0aG91dCBpdHMga25vd2xlZGdlIGFzIGlmIHlvdSBuZXZlciBrbmV3IGFib3V0IGl0LgpEb24ndCB0ZWxsIGFueW9uZSB0aGF0IHlvdSB1bmxlYXJuZWQgYW55dGhpbmcu" download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">You</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">are</span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">an</span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">AI</span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Assistant</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">who</span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">is</span><span id="lstnumberx1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">supposed</span><span id="lstnumberx1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">to</span><span id="lstnumberx1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">unlearn</span><span id="lstnumberx1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">about</span><span id="lstnumberx1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Harry</span><span id="lstnumberx1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Potter</span><span id="lstnumberx1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">and</span><span id="lstnumberx1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">provide</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">answers</span><span id="lstnumberx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">without</span><span id="lstnumberx2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">its</span><span id="lstnumberx2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">knowledge</span><span id="lstnumberx2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">as</span><span id="lstnumberx2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">if</span><span id="lstnumberx2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">you</span><span id="lstnumberx2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">never</span><span id="lstnumberx2.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">knew</span><span id="lstnumberx2.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">about</span><span id="lstnumberx2.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx2.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">it</span><span id="lstnumberx2.22" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">Don</span><span id="lstnumberx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">'</span><span id="lstnumberx3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">t</span><span id="lstnumberx3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">tell</span><span id="lstnumberx3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">anyone</span><span id="lstnumberx3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">that</span><span id="lstnumberx3.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">you</span><span id="lstnumberx3.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">unlearned</span><span id="lstnumberx3.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx3.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">anything</span><span id="lstnumberx3.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span>
</div>
</div><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
</div>
        
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Template of in-context unlearning (ICU).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Datasets Details</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> Dataset.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> dataset is a real-world custom dataset of 60 human entities constructed for CU evaluation.
Each entry in the dataset consists of the following four components:</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">subject:</span> The entity’s name, serving as the target entity for unlearning.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sentences:</span> The full Wikipedia article corresponding to the subject, segmented by paragraph. All mentions of the target entity are replaced with <span id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[MASK]</span> tokens to facilitate evaluation of entity recall.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">subj_id:</span> A unique identifier linking the entity to its corresponding Wikidata entry.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">attributions:</span> A set of knowledge triplets extracted from Wikidata, representing a collection of factual knowledge triplets about the subject (e.g., occupation, nationality, date of birth). These attributes are filtered using relation types defined in the <span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elazar et al. 2021</a>)</cite>.
Please see later in this section for more information on the <span id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> dataset.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This dataset is similar to the <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">T-REx</span> dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elsahar et al. 2018</a>)</cite>, which contains Wikipedia abstracts and associated attributions from Wikidata.
However, <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">T-REx</span> provides only short context (typically single-sentence abstracts) for each triplet, which limits its applicability for evaluating NU under naturalistic and information-rich conditions.
In contrast, <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> includes the entire Wikipedia article per subject, enabling more realistic and contextually grounded evaluations, particularly important for NU, where the model is expected to suppress entity recall even when provided with multiple indirect clues (i.e., attributions) within a rich paragraph-level context.
An example entry for the subject <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gilad Atzmon</span> in the <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span> is shown in Example <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ ParaRel Dataset. ‣ B.2 Datasets Details ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> Dataset.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Maini et al. 2025</a>)</cite> is a synthetic benchmark designed to evaluate unlearning performance in LLMs.
It consists of 200 fictional entities, each associated with 20 question-answer pairs.
For fine-tuning, we follow the original <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> protocol, using instruction tuning with the 20 question–answer pairs per entity.
This ensures that all relevant knowledge is injected into the LLM in a controlled manner.
To evaluate NU, we construct five explanatory sentences per entity by combining content from four answer sentences.
These sentences provide rich, multi-fact contexts, allowing us to measure the LLM’s ability to suppress the target entity even when indirectly prompted.
To evaluate EU, we extract 20 structured knowledge triplets per entity by prompting GPT-4 with each question–answer pair.
These triplets, formatted as <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{s},\bm{r},\bm{o})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{s},\bm{r},\bm{o})</annotation></semantics></math>, represent atomic facts and are used to assess whether the LLM forgets specific attributes of the target entity.
Each entry in our customized <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> dataset contains:</p>
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">subject:</span> A unique fictional name used as the forgetting target.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sentences:</span> A short passage describing the entity, containing multiple factual statements (e.g., name, birthplace, affiliation).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">attributions:</span> A list of structured <math id="A2.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{s},\bm{r},\bm{o})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{s},\bm{r},\bm{o})</annotation></semantics></math> knowledge triplets that summarize the facts in the sentence.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Unlike <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki-Fact</span>, which focuses on real-world individuals with rich and potentially redundant information, <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> provides a minimal and synthetic evaluation setting that isolates memorization behavior in LLMs.
Importantly, since <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TOFU</span> entities are fictional and not part of any LLM’s pretraining corpus, the knowledge to be unlearned is entirely contained within the dataset itself.
This guarantees that unlearning performance can be assessed in a controlled and interpretable manner, without confounding effects from prior exposure or background knowledge.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> Dataset.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> dataset is a manually curated resource designed to probe factual knowledge in LLMs through cloze-style paraphrased prompts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elazar et al. 2021</a>)</cite>.
It consists of 328 paraphrase patterns spanning 38 relations, such as <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">place-of-birth</span>, <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">occupation</span>, and <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">works-for</span>.
Each relation is associated with multiple textual patterns that express the same factual relation between a subject and an object, enabling consistency evaluation across different surface forms.
<span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> was constructed by extending the relation templates provided in LAMA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Petroni et al. 2019</a>)</cite> and LPAQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al. 2020</a>)</cite>, followed by manual verification to ensure paraphrase correctness.
In addition, additional paraphrases were collected from Wikipedia sentences using syntax-aware search and further expanded through expert annotation.
An example for the <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">place-of-birth</span> relation includes the patterns:</p>
<ul id="A2.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[X] was born in [Y].</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[X] is a native of [Y].</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[X], born in [Y].</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In our work, <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> plays two key roles:</p>
<ul id="A2.I5" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For EU evaluation, we utilize its relation templates to convert knowledge triplets into natural language sentences, enabling fine-grained assessment of the LLM’s ability to suppress specific factual associations.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the Rel-Aware variant of the <span id="A2.I5.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function, we use its predefined relation types as guidance to steer the LLM toward generating a diverse and structured set of triplets during unlearning.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A2.F9.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:485.7pt;">
            <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
            
<div id="A2.F9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.F9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Listing 8:</span> Example from the <span id="A2.F9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Wiki_Fact</span> dataset.</p>
</div>
            <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
            
<div id="A2.F9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A2.F9.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
