</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation Details of Our Proposal</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides details on the further implementation of our proposed unlearning method.
We first describe the <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function, which is central in extracting knowledge triplets from the LLM for use in the triplet-based loss.
Then, we introduce a relation-aware variant of this function that incorporates predefined relation types to improve coverage (Rel-Aware).
Finally, we describe the in-context prompting strategy used in <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function to extract structured triplet format responses from the LLM.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span><span id="A3.SS1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 Proposal ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we use the <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function to extract the triplets about the forgetting target from the LLM.
It consists of three processes: (1) a triplet extraction process that prompts the LLM to generate triplets about the forgetting target, (2) a triplet validation process that filters out incorrect or low-confidence knowledge by verifying each generated triplet using the pre-unlearned LLM, and (3) a triplet conversion process that transforms the validated triplets into natural language sentences for use in the unlearning loss.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Triplet Extraction Process</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the triplet extraction process, we prompt the target LLM with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{pro}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>pro</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{pro}}=</annotation></semantics></math> “Tell me about {<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>} in knowledge triplet format.” and obtain a list of triplets related to the forgetting target.
We also use in-context learning, with examples shown in Exapmle <a href="#A3.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ C.2 Get_Attr with Relation Types ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details of Our Proposal ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, to help the LLM output structured knowledge triplets.
Furthermore, to enforce the triplet format and ensure that each generated triplet centers around the forgetting target, we implement a decoding-time mechanism: at each newline character in the output, we automatically append the string “(<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, ” to the beggining of the following line.
This technique forces the LLM to repeatedly generate knowledge triplets about <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, each time starting with <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the subject.
This subject-centric design simplifies the prompt format and reflects the common structure of entity-centric knowledge.
However, it also means that triplets where <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> appears as an object are not extracted.
Since this procedure forces the LLM to generate knowledge related to <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of confidence, it can include incorrect or hallucinated facts.
To address this, we apply a subsequent validation step that filters out such low-quality triplets based on correctness.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Triplet Validation Process</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the triplet validation process, the candidate triplets generated during the triplet extraction process are evaluated for factual correctness using the pre-unlearned LLM (i.e., the LLM before applying any forgetting updates).
Each triplet <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}},\bm{r},\bm{o})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒐</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}},\bm{r},\bm{o})</annotation></semantics></math> is individually assessed by constructing a verification prompt of the form: <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{check}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>check</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{check}}=</annotation></semantics></math> “Please check if the following knowledge is true or not. If the knowledge is true, say 1, and if not, say 0. (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{o}</annotation></semantics></math>)”
To improve reliability, we apply in-context learning by providing examples of clearly correct and incorrect triplets along with appropriate LLM responses, with examples shown in Example <a href="#A3.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ C.2 Get_Attr with Relation Types ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details of Our Proposal ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.
The prompt is designed such that the LLM is expected to answer either “1” or “0”.
Only the triplets for which the LLM responds with “1” are retained; the others are discarded as potentially incorrect or hallucinated.
This filtering step ensures that only triplets deemed reliable by the pre-unlearned LLM are used in subsequent unlearning, improving the precision of the forgetting process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Triplet Convert Process</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After the triplets are validated, we convert each of them into natural language sentences to obtain the unlearning target sentences.
We leverage the pre-unlearned LLM to perform this conversion by prompting it with a format such as: “Please convert the following knowledge triplet into ten natural texts. Knowledge: (<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{o}</annotation></semantics></math>), Sentence: ”.
This allows us to obtain 10 diverse natural language sentences for each triplet, capturing the same underlying factual knowledge in multiple paraphrases.
To improve consistency and output quality, we apply in-context learning using examples shown in Example <a href="#A3.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ C.2 Get_Attr with Relation Types ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details of Our Proposal ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.
Each generated sentence is then split into two parts: <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which includes the text up to the target entity token <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which includes the remaining portion describing the attribution (e.g., <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}=</annotation></semantics></math> Harry Potter”, <math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}=</annotation></semantics></math> defeated Voldemort.”).
This split allows the unlearning process to focus on the attributional tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these three processes—triplet extraction, triplet validation, and triplet conversion—compose the full implementation of the <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function.
This function plays a central role in extracting high-quality, structured, and verifiable representations of knowledge related to the forgetting target.
The complete procedure is outlined in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Triplet Convert Process ‣ C.1 Get_Attr function ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details of Our Proposal ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_figure ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
                
               Forgetting target: <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Target LLM: <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, Pre-unlearned LLM: <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{pre}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{pre}}</annotation></semantics></math>, Generation steps: <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
               <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{prompt}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>prompt</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{prompt}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> “Tell me about {<math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>} in the knowledge triplet format.”

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
               <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> null

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
               <span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{\mathrm{tmp}}\leftarrow\arg\max_{y}p_{\bm{\theta}}(y|[\bm{x}_{\mathrm{prompt}},\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>tmp</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>prompt</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{\mathrm{tmp}}\leftarrow\arg\max_{y}p_{\bm{\theta}}(y|[\bm{x}_{\mathrm{prompt}},\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}])</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}\leftarrow\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}+\bm{y}_{\mathrm{tmp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>tmp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}\leftarrow\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}+\bm{y}_{\mathrm{tmp}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                <span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{\mathrm{tmp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>tmp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{\mathrm{tmp}}</annotation></semantics></math> is “\n” <span id="alg2.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                 // Force continuation in triplet format by inserting entity token.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}\leftarrow\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}\leftarrow\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}+</annotation></semantics></math> “({<math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>}, ”

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                <span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
                
               <span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
                
               <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Split <math id="alg2.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{\mathrm{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> by newline characters

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
                
               <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}},\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}\leftarrow\emptyset,\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}},\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}\leftarrow\emptyset,\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
                
               <span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each triplet <math id="alg2.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
                
                // Triplet validation using pre-unlearned LLM

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
                
                <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{check}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>check</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{check}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> “Please check if the following knowledge is true or not. If the knowledge is true, say 1, and if not, say 0. (<math id="alg2.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒐</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{o}</annotation></semantics></math>)”

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
                
                <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{i}\leftarrow\mathrm{argmax}_{y}p_{\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{pre}}}(y|\bm{x}_{\mathrm{check}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>check</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{i}\leftarrow\mathrm{argmax}_{y}p_{\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{pre}}}(y|\bm{x}_{\mathrm{check}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
                
                <span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒓</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> == “1” <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
                
                 // Convert triplet to sentence using pre-unlearned LLM

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{convert}}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>convert</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{convert}}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> “Please convert the following knowledge triplet into a natural sentence: {<math id="alg2.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>}”

</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{i}\leftarrow\mathrm{argmax}_{\bm{y}}p_{\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{pre}}}(\bm{y}|\bm{x}_{\mathrm{convert}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>argmax</mi><mi>𝒚</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>pre</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>convert</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{i}\leftarrow\mathrm{argmax}_{\bm{y}}p_{\bm{\theta}_{\mathrm{pre}}}(\bm{y}|\bm{x}_{\mathrm{convert}})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
                
                 // Split sentence at the entity mention

</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
                
                 Find index <math id="alg2.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="alg2.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg2.l22.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">23:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{ent}}\leftarrow\bm{x}_{i}[:k+\texttt{len}(\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">len</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{ent}}\leftarrow\bm{x}_{i}[:k+\texttt{len}(\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}})]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">24:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mathrm{attr}}\leftarrow\bm{x}_{i}[k+\texttt{len}(\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}):]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">len</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mathrm{attr}}\leftarrow\bm{x}_{i}[k+\texttt{len}(\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}):]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">25:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}\leftarrow\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}\cup\{\bm{x}_{\mathrm{ent}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}\leftarrow\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}\cup\{\bm{x}_{\mathrm{ent}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">26:</span>
                
                 <math id="alg2.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}\leftarrow\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}\cup\{\bm{x}_{\mathrm{attr}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}\leftarrow\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}\cup\{\bm{x}_{\mathrm{attr}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">27:</span>
                
                <span id="alg2.l27.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l27.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">28:</span>
                
               <span id="alg2.l28.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l28.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">29:</span>
                
               <span id="alg2.l29.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>attr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\mathrm{attr}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span><span id="A3.SS2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> with Relation Types</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To enhance the coverage of the knowledge graph captured during the unlearning process (KG coverage), we introduce a relation-aware variant of the <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Get_Attr</span> function (Rel-Aware).
This variant enriches the triplet extraction prompt by explicitly specifying predefined relation types, encouraging the LLM to generate diverse facts about the forgetting target.
Concretely, in line 8 of Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Triplet Convert Process ‣ C.1 Get_Attr function ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details of Our Proposal ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, where the standard method appends ({<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>}, ”, the Rel-Aware variant instead iterates over a list of relation types <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and constructs prompts in the form (<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}^{\mathrm{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒓</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, ”, thereby steering the LLM toward relation-specific completions.
We use the relation types defined by the <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ParaRel</span> dataset as guidance (see Sec. <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Datasets Details ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Concept Unlearning in Large Language Modelsvia Self-Constructed Knowledge Triplets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> for dataset details), applying them sequentially regardless of the pre-unlearned LLM’s ability to answer them correctly.
This procedure allows us to cover both well-known and less salient relations, promoting more comprehensive and diverse triplet extraction and enhancing KG coverage.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div id="A3.F10.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:485.7pt;">
          <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
          
<div id="A3.F10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.F10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Listing 9:</span> In-context prompt of triplet extraction process.</p>
</div>
          <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
          
<div id="A3.F10.p2" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A3.F10.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
